From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 20:22:52 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] btif: a2dp: Deepen the A2DP source TX queue to 112 frames

Streaming over busy Wi-Fi (video, for instance) holds the shared 2.4 GHz
antenna off Bluetooth long enough to overflow the 56-frame queue. Let it
hold 112 frames (~320 ms of SBC). The extra audio this can hold is
reported as delay by the next change, so players keep video in sync.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WBs6XUfh1pxQ1q9QJe6TLW
---
 system/btif/src/btif_a2dp_source.cc | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/system/btif/src/btif_a2dp_source.cc b/system/btif/src/btif_a2dp_source.cc
index 21d4994..7eaf0e1 100644
--- a/system/btif/src/btif_a2dp_source.cc
+++ b/system/btif/src/btif_a2dp_source.cc
@@ -79,7 +79,7 @@ using namespace bluetooth;
  * but due to link flow control or thread preemption in lower
  * layers we might need to temporarily buffer up data.
  */
-#define MAX_OUTPUT_A2DP_FRAME_QUEUE_SZ (MAX_PCM_FRAME_NUM_PER_TICK * 4)
+#define MAX_OUTPUT_A2DP_FRAME_QUEUE_SZ (MAX_PCM_FRAME_NUM_PER_TICK * 8)
 
 class SchedulingStats {
 public:
